The host program (ffgn) and the GPU engine (nebgpu: libnebgpu.so / nebgpu.dll) are original work; the host program is
built on the code base of the FreeForGem miner (common parts: pool failover, undervolt and clock control, idle mode,
auto-lock, status API). The GPU engine is distributed in binary form only. Parts of them are derived from, or built
with, the following third-party material, which remains under its own license.

* NEB reference implementation (C) -- from https://github.com/SilasEigen/neb release 1.0.0, commit
  feb0adac37af7e442f507c1853fc4b870137da06, folder pow/ref (blake3_min, chacha8, nebhash2, shares and the dataset helpers).
  Copyright the NEB authors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
  The files are unmodified. The miner compiles them in and uses them to compute again every nonce the GPU reports before it
  is sent, and as the reference of the self-test and of the undervolt checks. Parts of the GPU engine are derived from
  pow/gpu/nebhash2_cuda.cu of the same release (Apache-2.0). The layout of the work-service frames and the neb-pool/1
  client follow spec/node.md and spec/pool.md of the same release.

* Dataset file neb-datasets.bin (shipped in the packages) -- the dataset file of the NEB main network, unchanged from the
  NEB 1.0.0 release (222,320,684 bytes, SHA-256 500846f682669743b1305776cfbf19edc11ad3db1c809bd5a4fe5b33cf196fa4). It is
  derived from
    - the Kepler DR24 transit signals of the NASA Exoplanet Archive (NASA, https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu), and
    - OCTMNIST of MedMNIST v2 (Yang et al.), licensed under CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ ;
      the underlying images are from Kermany et al., "Identifying Medical Diagnoses and Treatable Diseases by Image-Based
      Deep Learning", Cell 172(5), 2018.
  See docs/mainnet.md and docs/testnet.md of the NEB release for how the file is made.

* Rust crates from crates.io (blake3, anyhow, serde_json, base64, rand, ctrlc, socket2, sha2, rustls, ring, webpki-roots,
  cc and their dependencies) -- each under its own license, typically MIT and/or
  Apache-2.0 (ring: ISC-style; webpki-roots carries the Mozilla CA certificate list, MPL-2.0 data). rustls provides the TLS
  of stratum+ssl:// pool connections.

* NVIDIA CUDA runtime (cudart) -- linked statically into libnebgpu.so / nebgpu.dll and redistributed under the NVIDIA CUDA
  Toolkit End User License Agreement. The CUDA driver (libcuda / nvcuda) is not distributed; it comes with the NVIDIA driver.

The NEB node and the wallet (neb-node, neb-wallet) are not part of these packages; they come from the official NEB release.
